{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks","id":661451,"title":"Werewolf Setting Hacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-11T21:19:51-07:00","id":661451,"title":"Werewolf Setting Hacks","content":"I've seen plenty of alternative settings for V:tM, though it seems like I don't see threads like that nearly as often for W:tA, even though I think that the game's setting might be really interesting to play around with. Has anyone ever created, or even run, an alternative Werewolf setting where some of the core aspects of the game have been changed?<br /> <br /> I personally have never rumor played in such a game, though I've had a few thoughts for alternate settings that might be interesting, at least as a short Chronicle or even just a though experiment. One idea being a version if Werewolf where the Weaver is seen as the main enemy instead of the Wyrm, where the primary enemy Tribe is the Glass Walkers instead f the Black Spiral Dancers. Another thought I had was for a Kinfolk based game set after all of the Garou have perished and only the Kinfolk remain to fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else created, played in, or thought about experimenting with W:tA's setting in such a way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:08:22-07:00","id":661723,"title":"","content":"I have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My brain is constantly coming up with ways to adapt or play around with the setting. I always go back though. To the actual setting as I love the gane itself.<br /> <br /> So I usually just do one off games of crossovers, what ifs, and 'this is bat $#!% cray cray...but let's see what happens!!!' Kinda stuff.<br /> <br /> examples include:<br /> <br /> What if ALIENS:<br /> Meteor crashes in new mexico. It devestates the area and the garou, though saddened and enraged by the desteuction are still kinda happy it took out a BSD hive. <br /> Our intrepid Troupe are the first to go in and check out. With hopes of Star Metal from the skies to make fetishes with and cleanse the remaining blights hoping with Rorgs touch to the lands the Wyld may still prevail now in the area. (Especially as no one even knew a meteor was headed this way, how random is that?!!)<br /> But it's not long till they start finding weird constructs like giant beehives being built up in the BSDs old tunnels and whole villages nearby missing its people. And mad graffiti depicting savage looking chubracabra with long tongues and no eyes and black bodies stealing people in the night.<br /> yep ALIENS are in WoD. I pur them in castes and types. Figured they were the spiritual remanant of the survivors of the weavers Insect Wars and been hiding way down deep in the Weavers realm cocooning and tainting others to breed more of their kind in deadly efficient and terrible ways of parasitic infestation. Until some went roaming and took on Rorg. Who quickly dispearsed them out of his realm on a meteor and decided to strike it at a hive that had also in the past given him trouble. Two birds one stone kinda thing.<br /> except some survived and now found thenselves physical rather than spiritual.<br /> they build the Hives to reconnect to the Weaver and her one song. Using the size of the hive as a booster of sorts. If one gets big enough it can exist in both umbra and physical realms and the Aliens can reconnect to the Weaver.<br /> The real horror kicked in when the Troupe found out what the surviving BSDs and wyrm tainted kinfolk host bodies created after face hugger fun times. Wyrm tainted Aliens who killed and destroyed and other things rather than secure and infect (on behalf of the Wyrm).<br /> The next terrible thing...where people and kin died after being chestbursted by baby Alien. Garou...regenerated...and where being infected again and again and again while webbed and fused and calicified to the Hive walls. Oh yeah...imagine that fate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I put in a whole mythology, purpose and reason, spirit broods and their relation to the Ananasae (The werespiders teeth had a natural resin that when used kept the Aliens blood non-acidic nor volatile and drinkinable..in fact twice as nourishing) but it didnt come up. The Garou all wanted an Alien Queens head as a trophy instead of finding out about them and pretty much just stormed a hive and went Vasquez and Drake on the whole thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:11:34-07:00","id":661725,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy created Guyver Units to take on the monsters and Deviants of the world but the three prototypes accidentally got out into the world..<br /> <br /> that was fun. Plus I found a fan site where someone had already applied lot of Guyver stuff into cWoD rules and stats (if you're the person who did that and you're out there...Thank you Loved it!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:19:29-07:00","id":661727,"title":"","content":"I also took Illiad and Odysseys work on behalf of Pentex and the Wyrm and turned them into a secret organisation that was recruiting people with special abilities and forging them into Superhero teams. <br /> <br /> Due to popularity of superheros, cosplay, comics and video games it seemed common sense the wyrm would want a piece of the Action.<br /> <br /> At firsr they are praised and treated especially well. Given every comfort, nifty gadget, armour, suits and promises of sponsorship and their own ranges of merch and fame.<br /> <br /> of course it all gets more and more sinister and corruptive from there. Enjoyed it a lot as did the players. I took a list of powers of wikipedia and combined them with fomori taint traits and powers.<br /> <br /> even had a few npcs who were more than willing to give them upgrades, DNA tweaks and implants (all experimental of course) while they took on the evil Anthromorph Aliens of the world that were set on destroying humanity, cities, homes and the corporations that allowed the Heros to live such wonderful lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:21:36-07:00","id":661730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=661727#post661727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also took Illiad and Odysseys work on behalf of Pentex and the Wyrm and turned them into a secret organisation that was recruiting people with special abilities and forging them into Superhero teams.<br /> <br /> Due to popularity of superheros, cosplay, comics and video games it seemed common sense the wyrm would want a piece of the Action.<br /> <br /> At firsr they are praised and treated especially well. Given every comfort, nifty gadget, armour, suits and promises of sponsorship and their own ranges of merch and fame.<br /> <br /> of course it all gets more and more sinister and corruptive from there. Enjoyed it a lot as did the players. I took a list of powers of wikipedia and combined them with fomori taint traits and powers.<br /> <br /> even had a few npcs who were more than willing to give them upgrades, DNA tweaks and implants (all experimental of course) while they took on the evil Anthromorph Aliens of the world that were set on destroying humanity, cities, homes and the corporations that allowed the Heros to live such wonderful lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, back then when the first teasers of the setting were still coming up but the book wasn't out, i thought <b>Aberrant</b> was supposed to be that... The fact the Novas' main problem was the <b>taint</b> of their power and its misuse - and that Freak Legion called stat-enhancements &quot;mega-attributes&quot; only made the association more ridiculously simple. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> About alt stuff my own, I wouldn't call it a <b>core</b> change, but recently i got in a mood to look into australian folklore for color in writing some oWoD stuff and the more i read it, the more it felt to me lke the Bunyip were a misstep - not for the whole &quot;tasmanian wolf as garou&quot; gonzo-ness per se, but because the bunyip critter itself is a pretty terrible choice for association, a nocturnal predator of animals, women &amp; children that hides in rivers, creeks and waterholes during the day hour, something i would connect more to some savage kindred alternate form than garou. Meanwhile the Dirawong and Rainbow Serpent make a much stronger case for Mokole as prime shapeshifter of pre-european settling Australia.<br /> <br /> It's has all kind of come up to me during the last week, so it's not like i have done anything about it, but i'm tempted to give Rage Across Australia a good long read and see how would things change with no &quot;14<sup>th</sup> tribe&quot; and mokole as original aboriginal wardens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-12-2015, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:35:37-07:00","id":661742,"title":"","content":"I also put together a European version of the Kitsune (I love the game but never really wanted to use the Kitsune for anything personally). So I based a bunch of hidden fera red haired werefoxes based on old euro myth lore and written works.<br /> <br /> They werent on good terms with Uncle Wolf so mostlt hid from the others. And while madated not to wipe out humanity they didnt aplreciate their fox stock being hunted across europe so much by the rich and privileged.<br /> still with Cunning, Glory and Honor, they commit to 'Shenanigans' which are usually long cons over the rich, privileged and greedy. Though tend to end up with 'Stores' and 'larders' in fheir dens that they dont know what to do with once they have so much.<br /> They get a bit exciteable. But who can not like a fox in a monocle who's conned his way into marrying into the uppercrust of society to take what they have...and maybe give to others less fortunate. Trick the Wyrm (wealth, greed, destruction etc) for Glory, Share the Wealth for Honor, Learn and Teach for Wisdom.<br /> With only a few spirit totems so far since they came in after the war of tears. Red Fox, City Fox, Dog, Alley Cat and The Red Squirrel (they like Raven...but that guy wont keep his mouth shut if they let him know they are there.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:50:04-07:00","id":661758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=661742#post661742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also put together a European version of the Kitsune (I love the game but never really wanted to use the Kitsune for anything personally). So I based a bunch of hidden fera red haired werefoxes based on old euro myth lore and written works.<br /> <br /> They werent on good terms with Uncle Wolf so mostlt hid from the others. And while madated not to wipe out humanity they didnt aplreciate their fox stock being hunted across europe so much by the rich and privileged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, fox-hunting has gone considerably out of fashion with the years actually. Not like there's much bragging to be had on one's guts and boldness in catching that widdle fox pelt, i guess.<br /> <br /> Also, urban foxes have became a thing in the last century, at least in England. <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/uk/shortcuts/2013/feb/11/urban-foxes-fact-fiction\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s an article having a bit of fun on local fact and fiction over the subject (awesome fodder for games centered on &quot;Renards&quot; i would say).<br /> <br /> In Siberia meanwhile, things have taken an even more <a href=\"http://www.popsci.com/science/article/2012-10/fyi-domesticated-foxes\" target=\"_blank\">peculiar turn</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-12-2015, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:00:25-07:00","id":661763,"title":"","content":"I'm British, so I know of this :-) thanks tho. It's good for others. I put the changes of 'being now out of fashion' due to the Red Folk infiltrating high society and taking it down from the inside. From human stock marrying their way into riches and political halls, joining fringe groups and adopting thenselves into anything that has the potential to change or teach. Whether 'Anonymous'ly over the internet, Renyard-esque courtly love affairs and being a 'Menace' on behalf of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> you gotta have a Reynard faction with European foxes right? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7706,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","user":"Somuchlove","date":". 09-12-2015, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:11:22-07:00","id":661773,"title":"","content":"I might have even put in a joke where one Fox in particular had done so much courting and philandering with royal circles there's a rumour one of his offspring is actially in line (to a degree) to the royal throne of England.<br /> <br /> of course all eyes are open for a red haired child of fox who seems to be more prone to mockery and jest than anything serious within royalty....ahem...(spoiler..it's Harry ;-) )<br /> <br /> of course this is just a prank and nothing more than a light hearted jest itself than suggest anything improper or disrespectful to anyone real....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:50:43-07:00","id":661920,"title":"","content":"Just took a look at a review of Rage Across Australia and if i had any doubts about that i was going into a pretty different direction, they are mostly gone indeed.<br /> Didn't remember how cringe-worthy some stuff there was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T08:20:25-07:00","id":661930,"title":"","content":"While we're on the topic of Australia: A post-apocalyptic setting inspired by Mad Max might be fun. What happens when the war for Gaia is definitely lost, but werewolves are still around and the winning faction finds out that a world in ruins isn't quite as glorious as they thought it would be?<br /> Of course, you'd probably have to handwave some excuse for the PCs to drive around in a gas-guzzling behemoth, but I'm sure some Glass Walkers (Rust Riders?) with a clean energy source could manage something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T08:26:03-07:00","id":661933,"title":"","content":"Rust Riders???? Love it!!! Maybe they are Bonegnawers in my brain tho<br /> <br /> but love it!<br /> <br /> And yes, Werewolf after Apocalypse needs Mad Max like stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:59:55-07:00","id":662178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=661930#post661930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the topic of Australia: A post-apocalyptic setting inspired by Mad Max might be fun. What happens when the war for Gaia is definitely lost, but werewolves are still around and the winning faction finds out that a world in ruins isn't quite as glorious as they thought it would be?<br /> Of course, you'd probably have to handwave some excuse for the PCs to drive around in a gas-guzzling behemoth, but I'm sure some Glass Walkers (Rust Riders?) with a clean energy source could manage something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just motors with more efficient philtering of its emissions might be good enough depending on individual garou attitude, honestly. That said combustion engines fueled by ethanol or other substances of vegetable/renewable origin <b>already</b> exist in some countries and have been a thing in Brazil for more about 40 years.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, i would be all for the Rust Riders as some hybrid tribe borne out of Glass Walker &amp; Bone Gnawer remnants both.<br /> The world changed why would the tribes not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-12-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T15:11:38-07:00","id":662259,"title":"","content":"@Baaldam<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, just motors with more efficient philtering of its emissions might be good enough depending on individual garou attitude, honestly. That said combustion engines fueled by ethanol or other substances of vegetable/renewable origin <b>already</b> exist in some countries and have been a thing in Brazil for more about 40 years. </div> </div> </div>While technically correct, those substances aren't without their own problems - corn has to be planted somewhere and &quot;somewhere&quot; often happens to be former rainforest. And of course, it still runs into the problem of every post-apocalyptic setting: On the one hand, it's a setting of extreme scarcity, where it's entirely possible to run out of bullets, to starve to death or die from thirst. On the other hand, the protagonists and antagonists should be able to sustain cars which need either oil for gas (meaning the whole &quot;post peak oil&quot; thing isn't quite as post as most of the background would suggest) or biofuel (meaning there's a lot of farming around which could easily produce enough food for people).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, i would be all for the Rust Riders as some hybrid tribe borne out of Glass Walker &amp; Bone Gnawer remnants both.<br /> The world changed why would the tribes not? </div> </div> </div>Hybrid tribes sound good, but I'd rather hybridize others. GWs and BGs are presently the only two tech-friendly tribes, something that works very well in the setting. Other tribes may lose their focus - when there's no Garou Nation to lead anymore, the Silver Fangs lose one of their key concepts - and may thus benefit more strongly from merging with another tribe that fit better into the setting.<br /> Conceptwise, I'd see the Bone Gnawers more grounded in the here-and-now while the descendants of the Glass Walkers range either into the past or the future. Gnawers improvise with what they have at hand whereas Glass Walkers either research new technologies or mount expeditions to regain functional pre-Apocalypse tech.<br /> <br /> ...I think I might have to go write some stuff down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T15:41:41-07:00","id":662309,"title":"","content":"What of making the Black furies a feminist tribe that doesn't slaughter their male Garou children or tell them to go screw off and live with the Children of Gaia? <br /> <br /> One thing I am curious about is the idea of making the Nagah more known to other fera. How would this fact change things if they were more known among the fera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:46:19-07:00","id":662411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=662309#post662309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I am curious about is the idea of making the Nagah more known to other fera. How would this fact change things if they were more known among the fera?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh hi guys with short fuses well known for killing stuff they don't like, we are the secret police that has been hiding from you for all this time and we're actually killing the ones among you that we have decided are bad. Now let's just be friends&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:20:22-07:00","id":662428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=662309#post662309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What of making the Black furies a feminist tribe that doesn't slaughter their male Garou children or tell them to go screw off and live with the Children of Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would totally break with the greek myth amazons' connection that is behind it? That said having male packs, that fit into centaur imagery/tropes could be a curious angle, but would require some working to go well, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:13:10-07:00","id":662538,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of there being other Kitsune outside of Asia since there are a lot of fox legends and tales to draw from. (There's also the fennec and bat-eared foxes of Africa.) I'm sure the marble fox which was breed for it's unique fur color would have its own unique views on humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:02:18-07:00","id":663170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/661451-werewolf-setting-hacks?p=662538#post662538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of there being other Kitsune outside of Asia since there are a lot of fox legends and tales to draw from. (There's also the fennec and bat-eared foxes of Africa.) I'm sure the marble fox which was breed for it's unique fur color would have its own unique views on humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is the choice to limit werefoxes to kitsune might relate at least in part to frequent association of shapeshifting foxes with fae in european legends such as Reynardine.<br /> So basically the Pooka ruined everything forever for Fera or vice-versa, take your pick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:35:47-07:00","id":663603,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s my (long) one : <b>Mental Wyrm</b> <hr /><br /> Some time ago. Perhaps at the dawn of the Industrial Age perhaps scant decades ago, the Wyrm was wounded in its very essence.<br /> <br /> Four Packs, heroes and legends all of them embarked on a mighty quest: To slay the Elemental Wyrm and thus pave the way to the destruction or redemption of Ga\u00efa\u2019s balance. Long were these quests, paved with corruption and bloodshed. The packs were forced to replace their membership several times along the way until they were only legacies, four groups of werewolves determined to slay the Four Lords.<br /> <br /> The First Pack called Desirable Dominion decided to war against smoke-crowned Choke whose touch deludes and beffudles those whose lungs and skins are not gnawed by the acrid Smog. Persuaded the airy parts of the Wyrm could clear the skies of the material world of their filth, or at least not despoil them more, the pack spoke to many lords and ladies of air, reminding them of their obligation to Ga\u00efa. By guile, force, cajoling and threatening they assembled a mighty host of the mightiest air spirits that ever were. This same guile and quickness of thought enabled them to bring their forces to Choke\u2019s domain and engage in battle. The Lord of Smog was torn apart by his many foes, his essence dispersed to the sixty-four directions and thus, no Maeljin took his place.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Second Pack called Best Righteousness decided to war against balefire-cloaked Kerne whose touch brings no renewal only lingering death and pure destruction. Persuaded that the fiery parts of the Wyrm could be returned to their role as purifiers, they consulted many oracles to know their course. They learned no force in the world of spirits could destroy Lord Kerne, yet despite all warnings and the cries of their kin, they travelled to his castle of radioactive flame. There they fought him ten days and ten nights before encasing him in chains of lead. While the rogue spirit boasted no matter could resist his touch, the pack opened a gateway to the World of the Dead where all flame is stilled. Thus, the fury of Balefire was calmed and no Maeljin rose to this station.<br /> <br /> The Third Pack called Wholeness decided to war against fertile Yul whose womb endlessly spawn the abominations of the Wyrm and whose touch fouls the clearest water in poisonous liquid. Persuaded that the watery part of the Wyrm would once again give life and wash away corruption rather than foul and corrupt, the pack wandered far in search of a means to poison the poisoner. What they used in their mixture is unknown but tales are told of their travels through the worlds to harvest the purest ingredients until they submitted their creation to the madness of the Flux Realm. Whatever they put in the silver cup they brought to Malfeas, this was life in its rawest form. Lady Yul drank this potion and knew what she once forgot, love, emotions, purity and thus the toxins of Waasha were cleansed and no Maeljin held power over them.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Pack called Holy Devotion decided to war against sterile Lord Collum who gives no life and makes the earth bear no plants but creates more and more of itself until the universe is Sludge. Persuaded that the earthen parts of the Wyrm could heal what they once destroyed and bare life where they supported none, the pack wandered in search of secrets seeds to plant in the most desolate grounds. One they found on Earth, the second they took in Pangea, the third they created by magic and science wielded together, the fourth was brought by human will and the fifth took roots in one of their members. And all these plants they managed to fix to the Maeljin himself, looking as the sewage creature became the most powerful plant elemental to ever walk. No Maeljin claimed the throne of Sludge after that.<br /> <br /> And at the moment they did all this (because like in all legends they killed their Maeljin at the same time), the corrupt elements of the Wyrm became pure again. They became purifiers again, lost in a land of corruption. Uncountable billions of Wyrm creatures, Banes and twisted living things died in this instant, consumed in blind and howling agony as the elements ravaged all that was physical in Malfeas. In the material plane, sorcerers and Black Spiral Dancers were consumed by the very powers they tried to summon. In the end Malfeas still stood, for Lies, Desire, Parano\u00efa and Despair are not so easily defeated. However it was a land of nightmare for all corrupt being, walled off by angry elements now beyond corruption.<br /> <br /> But, the Garou Nation has far from won. While environmental pollution is no longer a top priority for the servants of Corruption, they remain in the world twisting minds rather than twisting bodies. If sludge, oil or smog were not enemies to be clawed on, what can be said of Hatred, of racism, of depression or madness? The Garou have less physical enemies to fight but the Wyrm is more cunning than ever and its servants subtler.<br /> <br /> Also what the Garou knows not, what perhaps not even the servants of the Dragon know not, it\u2019s that the madness of the Destroyer has receded. He still seeks to escape his prison by destroying the world but no longer his heads work at cross-purpose. He has a goal now, clear and unclouded sight, peerless passion and understanding of all emotions.<br /> <br /> It will be free. <hr /><br /> So<br /> <br /> No more Elemental Wyrms or pollution Cultists<br /> <br /> But plenty of Bale Hounds style cults, daemonic conspiracies, covert war against the ideals of humanity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T08:10:04-07:00","id":664322,"title":"","content":"One idea that came up to me of late, inspired by a discussion of oWoD terms littered here and there in Exalted, is sketching up some form of actual connection between the Malfeans from Wraith, the cthonic powers of Oblivion worshipped by the spectres in the Labyrinth and the realm of Malfeas. The two possible takes i'm still wrestling with are:<br /> <br /> 1) The malfeans are banes, Maejlin and other agents of the Wyrm infiltrating the Underworld, through the Abyss or similar place/force. In this context Underworld is one necessary step in the spiritual growth and eventual evolution of the most strong-willed of the dead into ancestor-spirits, something the malfean interference has twisted with time, breaking the familial and lineal ties across generations and cultures of humans in the ensuing centuries, a process the &quot;willful dead&quot; have had to fight on their own due to the lack of familiarity of the shapeshifters with their realm.<br /> <br /> 2) The malfeans are alien beings the<i> dead original natives of Malfeas</i>, a tellurian to be consumed/taken over by the Wyrm before the one we know. Their people, predators, guardians, guides, spirits, elementals, totems... remnants of these and more persist as angry shadows of their former selves in the Labyrinth, enclosed by bothersome outsiders even in their defeat and rest outside their lost home, now the throne-realm of their past nemesis and destroyer...<br /> <br /> Those are the concepts i cooked up last weekend, but i'm still kind of uncertain of which one to go with and how to expand them, though the first one <b>does</b> seem quicker to turn in a game as it would call for developing less stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-18-2023, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}